    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4648",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question refers to the following information.\nRead the the following quotation to answer questions.\nThe various modes of worship which prevailed in the Roman world were all considered by the people as equally true; by the philosopher as equally false; and by the magistrate as equally useful.\nEdward Gibbon, The Decline and Fall of the Roman Empire, 1776–1788\nGibbon's interpretation of the state of religious worship in ancient Rome could be summarized as\n\nOptions: \nA. In ancient Rome, religious worship was solely a matter of personal choice and preference.\nB. In ancient Rome, religious worship was seen as a moral obligation by the citizens.\nC. In ancient Rome, religious worship was heavily influenced by Greek mythology.\nD. In ancient Rome, religious worship was the source of much social tension and turmoil.\nE. In ancient Rome, religious worship was homogeneous and highly centralized.\nF. In ancient Rome, religious worship was decentralized and tended to vary with one's social position.\nG. In ancient Rome, religious worship was strictly enforced by the state.\nH. In ancient Rome, religious worship was considered to be a matter of political importance.\nI. In ancient Rome, religious worship was revolutionized by the introduction of Christianity.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Gibbon's quote highlights three distinct perspectives on Roman religious worship: the people saw it as equally true, philosophers as equally false, and the magistrate as equally useful. This indicates a pragmatic approach to religion, where its value was judged by its utility rather than its inherent truth. The quote suggests a lack of unified belief and a varied perception of religion's role across different social strata.\n\nLet's analyze the options:\nA. \"Solely a matter of personal choice and preference\" is too narrow; Gibbon mentions utility for the magistrate and philosophical skepticism.\nB. \"Moral obligation\" is not explicitly stated.\nC. \"Heavily influenced by Greek mythology\" is not mentioned in the quote.\nD. \"Source of much social tension and turmoil\" is not supported by the quote.\nE. \"Homogeneous and highly centralized\" is directly contradicted by the diverse perspectives presented.\nF. \"Decentralized and tended to vary with one's social position\" aligns well with the idea that different groups (people, philosophers, magistrates) had different views, implying variations based on social standing and a lack of a single, overarching dogma.\nG. \"Strictly enforced by the state\" is not indicated; the magistrate saw it as \"equally useful,\" suggesting functionality rather than strict enforcement of belief.\nH. \"Matter of political importance\" is partially supported by the magistrate's view of utility, but it doesn't capture the full nuance.\nI. \"Revolutionized by the introduction of Christianity\" is anachronistic to the general statement about prevalent worship and not directly addressed.\n\nOption F best summarizes the varied and non-uniform nature of religious worship described by Gibbon, where different classes held contrasting views on its truth and importance.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{F}$.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 322,
        "output_tokens": 367,
        "total_tokens": 689
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
    },
    "cost": null,
    "accuracy": null
  },
  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4674",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question refers to the following information.\nBECAUSE no People can be truly happy, though under the greatest Enjoyment of Civil Liberties, if abridged of the Freedom of their Consciences, as to their Religious Profession and Worship: And Almighty God being the only Lord of Conscience, Father of Lights and Spirits; and the Author as well as Object of all divine Knowledge, Faith and Worship, who only doth enlighten the Minds, and persuade and convince the Understanding of People, I do hereby grant and declare, That no Person or Persons, inhabiting in this Province or Territories, who shall confess and acknowledge One almighty God, the Creator, Upholder and Ruler of the World; and profess him or themselves obliged to live quietly under the Civil Government, shall be in any Case molested or prejudiced, in his or their Person or Estate, because of his or their conscientious Persuasion or Practice, nor be compelled to frequent or maintain any religious Worship, Place or Ministry, contrary to his or their Mind.…\n—William Penn, Charter of Privileges Granted by William Penn,\nesq. to the Inhabitants of Pennsylvania and Territories, October 28, 1701\nBecause of Penn's Charter of Privileges, Pennsylvania became\n\nOptions: \nA. a colony that banned all forms of religious expression.\nB. one of the least religiously diverse colonies in America.\nC. one of the most religiously diverse colonies in British America.\nD. known for its strict adherence to a single religious doctrine.\nE. known for its hostility to traditional religious practices.\nF. a colony that forbade the practice of any religion other than Christianity.\nG. a colony known for religious repression and intolerance.\nH. notorious for witch hunting and popular superstition.\nI. the only colony in America where religion was not practiced.\nJ. a colony where religious diversity was punishable by law.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The provided text, William Penn's Charter of Privileges, explicitly grants freedom of conscience and religious practice to those who acknowledge one Almighty God and live under civil government. This charter aimed to prevent the molestation or prejudice of individuals based on their religious beliefs or practices, and to ensure they were not compelled to support religious worship contrary to their minds. Therefore, Pennsylvania was established with a strong emphasis on religious liberty and tolerance.\n\nConsidering the provisions of the Charter of Privileges, we can evaluate the given options:\nA. This is incorrect, as the charter promotes religious freedom, not a ban on all religious expression.\nB. This is incorrect. The charter's commitment to religious freedom would attract people of various faiths, leading to diversity, not lack thereof.\nC. This is the most likely answer. By protecting freedom of conscience, Penn attracted a wide array of religious groups seeking refuge from persecution, making Pennsylvania highly religiously diverse.\nD. This is incorrect. The charter allows for diverse religious practices, not adherence to a single doctrine.\nE. This is incorrect. The charter is a document of religious freedom and tolerance, not hostility.\nF. This is incorrect. While it acknowledges one Almighty God, it doesn't restrict freedom to only Christianity.\nG. This is incorrect. The charter is fundamentally about religious tolerance and freedom from repression.\nH. This option refers to historical events largely unrelated to Penn's charter and its direct consequences.\nI. This is incorrect. The charter specifically addresses religious worship and practice, indicating religion was indeed practiced.\nJ. This is incorrect. The charter explicitly protects religious diversity, rather than punishing it.\n\nThe most likely correct answer is C.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{C}$.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 443,
        "output_tokens": 357,
        "total_tokens": 800
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
    },
    "cost": null,
    "accuracy": null
  },
