      "generated_answer": "Frederick Douglass was most influenced by the abolitionist movement, which sought to end slavery and promote equal rights for African Americans. His writings and advocacy were centered around the fight against slavery and for the liberation of enslaved people. This is evidenced by his focus on the \"crying curse of human bondage\" in the provided passage.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
