      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. The Treaty of Nanjing established spheres of influence for British trade in specific Chinese cities, allowing British merchants to operate with relative autonomy under British supervision. This arrangement laid the groundwork for increased British commercial privileges in China during the 19th century.",
