      "generated_answer": "The views expressed in the excerpt are best seen as evidence of which of the following in Roman society?\n\nOptions: \nA. Disgust for barbarian peoples\nB. Concern about barbarian attacks\nC. Absence of Stoicism among the aristocracy\nD. Maintenance of large armies\n\nThe correct letter choice is \\boxed{B}.\n\nThe excerpt highlights a calculated Roman preference for discord among neighboring barbarian tribes, which reflects concern about potential attacks, as their infighting distracted them from posing a united threat to Rome. Tacitus expresses appreciation for tribal conflicts as these prevent unified barbarian opposition to Roman expansion or power.",
