      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}. \n\nA sympathetic reader of Logan's Address would likely support respecting Indian territory and sovereignty, as Logan expresses a desire for peace and highlights the injustices faced by his people due to violence against them. The emphasis on his previous friendship and peaceful intentions towards whites contrasts sharply with the behavior of settlers, indicating a call for mutual respect rather than extermination or assimilation.",
