      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{J}. The Navigation Acts of 1651 aimed to curtail Dutch maritime dominance and facilitate English control over trade routes between England and its colonies, as well as manage imports from other countries. This legislation was part of broader economic and strategic efforts to strengthen England's position in global trade.",
