      "generated_answer": "The Native American Graves Protection and Repatriation Act (NAGPRA) specifically addresses ethical concerns and legal rights surrounding Native American human remains and associated funerary objects. Problems often arise when the spiritual beliefs and cultural practices of Native Americans are disregarded by archaeologists. Option C directly addresses this clash in understanding and respect, which is a common point of contention in the application of NAGPRA.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{C}$.",
